privacy.description:
The bot only uses slash commands: it **does not read** messages continuously.

**What is stored, per server:**
• warnings (`/warn`): member, moderator, reason, date;
• sanction history (warn, mute, kick, ban…): member, moderator, reason, duration, date (2 years max);
• ongoing temporary bans (end date);
• giveaways (entrants, winners: 30 days after the end) and scheduled announcements (until they are sent);
• ticket tracking: author, staff member who claimed it, dates, 1 to 5 rating (90 days after deletion; never the content);
• settings: log channel, tickets, automatic sanctions, locked channels, language, colour, panel texts;
• the last time a ticket was opened (erased within about 24 h).

Ticket transcripts are not kept by the bot: they are sent to the server's log channel.

**Retention:** as long as the bot is on the server. If it is removed, everything is erased **30 days** later. Daily database backups are kept for a few days (7 by default) and then replaced.
**Immediate erasure:** an administrator can use `/privacy supprimer:True`.

